*   **Low and Lower-Middle Income Settings (LIC/LMIC):** Focus on low-technology, human-resource-optimized interventions such as *Carer Transition Navigators (1.3)*, *Proactive Frailty Identification (2.2)*, *Offline Paper-Digital Summaries (6.3)*, and basic *Staff Rest Facilities (9.3)*. These models rely on operational coordination rather than expensive capital build-outs.
*   **Upper-Middle and High-Income Settings (UMIC/HIC):** Well-suited to capital-intensive, tech-driven models, including *Continuous Remote Patient Monitoring (5.1)*, *Universal Shared Care Record Integration (6.2)*, *Expanded Hospital SDEC Capacity (4.1)*, and *High-Street Point-of-Care Diagnostics (3.3)*.

